<title>USA: Edison Brothers extends voting deadline.</title>
<headline>Edison Brothers extends voting deadline.</headline>
<dateline>ST. LOUIS 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Edison Brothers Stores Inc said Friday it has extended the deadline for creditors and equity holders to vote on the company's plan of reorganization by one week.</p>
<p>The extension was made because the retailer realized it had not given enough time for shareholders to review the plan and vote, a spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>The company, which is currently under Chapter 11 bankruptcy protection, said the new deadline is 1600 CDT on August 4.</p>
<p>	 ((--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
